+//     all ones. draw_util::GetNormalizedColorMask is 0 unless RB_MODECONTROL is kColorDepth, the pixel shader
+//     statically writes the target and RB_COLOR_MASK enables a component the format has; 0 without a pixel shader.
+// (2) No depth or stencil stored. FSI_DepthStencilTest (spirv_translator_rb.cpp) stores a sample's depth / stencil
+//     only if the new value differs from the old one. The depth part changes only with kSysFlag_FSIDepthWrite,
